<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Societe Generale to buy S.African brokers - paper.</title>
<headline>Societe Generale to buy S.African brokers - paper.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French banking group Societe Generale is set to buy South African broking firm Frankel Pollak during the next week, local paper Business Day on Tuesday quoted market sources as saying.</p>
<p>Sources said the transaction was &quot;as good as done&quot; and only technicalities remained.</p>
<p>The talk surfaced ahead of a media briefing on Wednesday announced by Societe Generale.</p>
<p>Frankel Pollak chief executive Sidney Frankel declined to comment on Monday, Business Day said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
